### How DI works for MCP tools

The SDK supports **two injection styles**:

| Style | How it works |
|-------|-------------|
| **Constructor injection** (non-static class) | DI services in the constructor, tool params on methods. Class is instantiated per-call. |
| **Method parameter injection** (static class) | DI services as method parameters alongside tool params. SDK distinguishes them by type — registered services are injected, everything else becomes schema params. |

**Key rule:** `CancellationToken`, `IMcpServer`, `IProgress<T>`, and any DI-registered service are **auto-injected** and hidden from the LLM schema. Only `[Description]`-annotated parameters are visible.

